# command-wait

Inputs:

- workdir: `{{ run.workdir }}`
- notepad: `{{ run.workdir }}/notepad.md`

## Task

Ask the user for their next command. Classify it as `question`, `action`, or
`end`:

- `question` — the user is asking. Answer inline; no side effects.
- `action` — the user wants work done. Propose a kebab-case slug for the
  sub-folder name (e.g. `refactor-parser`, `add-timeout`).
- `end` — the user is closing the session.

## Output

```bash
LOOM=~/.kiro/skills/home/loom/scripts/loom.sh
$LOOM output init "{{ run.workdir }}" --task command-wait
$LOOM output add  "{{ run.workdir }}" --task command-wait \
    --set kind=<question|action|end> \
    --set command='<verbatim user text>' \
    --set slug='<slug-or-empty>'
```
